# Online Mafia Game - Cursor Rules

> **Read `/docs/README.md` before implementing features or fixing bugs.**

## Quick Reference

- **`/docs/README.md`** - Entry point (start here)
- **`/docs/architecture.md`** - Stack, boundaries, data flow
- **`/docs/realtime.md`** - Convex reactive queries (real-time)
- **`/docs/game-design.md`** - Mafia rules, phases, visibility
- **`/docs/frontend.md`** - React / UI conventions
- **`/docs/backend.md`** - Server patterns
- **`/docs/server-time.md`** - Server-corrected client clock for timers
- **`/docs/decisions.md`** - Architectural decisions (ADR)

## Core Stack

- **Framework**: Next.js 15 (App Router)
- **Database & Backend**: Convex (document DB + server functions)
- **Authentication**: Convex Auth (`@convex-dev/auth` with Password + Resend OTP)
- **Real-time**: Convex reactive queries (`useQuery` auto-updates)
- **Video/Audio**: LiveKit (WebRTC)
- **Styling**: TailwindCSS + shadcn/ui
- **Validation**: Zod (client), Convex validators (server)
- **Language**: TypeScript (strict mode)

## Key Principles

1. **All game logic in Convex functions**: `mutation` for writes, `query` for reads
2. **Reactive queries for real-time**: `useQuery` auto-syncs -- no manual subscriptions
3. **Type safety**: Use `Doc<"tableName">` from `convex/_generated/dataModel`
4. **Auth in every function**: `getAuthUserId(ctx)` at the start of mutations/queries
5. **Transactional mutations**: Convex mutations are atomic (full success or full rollback)
6. **Component composition**: Small, reusable components
7. **Custom hooks**: Extract data fetching into hooks under `src/hooks`
8. **Role-based visibility**: Game phase and role determine what players see
9. **Server-corrected time on client**: Use `useServerTime()` from `@/lib/time/serverTime` for any timer math against a server-issued timestamp. Never use raw `Date.now()` / `new Date()` for elapsed time on the client (see `/docs/server-time.md`)

## What We Do NOT Use

- `"use server"` server actions for game logic (use Convex mutations)
- `useEffect` for data subscriptions (use `useQuery`)
- Redux / Zustand (Convex reactive queries are the state)
- Socket.IO / Redis
- Custom WebRTC (use LiveKit)

## Before Implementing

1. Read relevant documentation in `/docs`
2. Check existing patterns in similar features
3. Use `Doc<"tableName">` types from `convex/_generated/dataModel`
4. Run `npx tsc` after changes to catch type errors
5. Follow component and hook patterns from existing code

## File Structure

- `/convex` - All backend logic (schema, mutations, queries)
- `/src/app` - Next.js App Router pages
- `/src/components` - React components (organized by feature)
- `/src/hooks` - Custom React hooks
- `/src/lib` - Utilities, constants, context
- `/src/lib/constants/game.ts` - Game constants (phases, roles, statuses)
- `/src/lib/game/visibility.ts` - Visibility logic (pure functions)
- `/src/lib/time/serverTime.ts` - `useServerTime()` for server-corrected client clock

## Type Safety

- Use `Doc<"tableName">` and `Id<"tableName">` from `convex/_generated/dataModel`
- Use `v.id("tableName")` for references in Convex schema
- Run `npx tsc` after every change
- Avoid `any` types
- Use strict TypeScript

## Real-time Updates

- Use `useQuery(api.tableName.queryName, args)` for reactive data
- Use `"skip"` for conditional queries: `useQuery(api.x.y, condition ? { id } : "skip")`
- `useQuery` returns `undefined` while loading
- No `useEffect`, no cleanup, no channel management

## Convex Functions

- All game logic in Convex `mutation` / `query` functions
- Authenticate with `getAuthUserId(ctx)` from `@convex-dev/auth/server`
- Use `ctx.db.get()`, `ctx.db.query()`, `ctx.db.insert()`, `ctx.db.patch()`, `ctx.db.delete()`
- Mutations throw errors on failure (caught by `useMutation` on frontend)
- Use `internalAction` for external API calls (LiveKit)

## Component Patterns

- Extract logic to custom hooks
- Keep components focused on UI
- Use shadcn/ui components from `/src/components/ui`
- Support dark mode
- Don't define helper functions inside components (use `/src/lib/utils`)

## Game Logic

- Game phases defined in `/src/lib/constants/game.ts`
- Visibility rules in `/src/lib/game/visibility.ts`
- Role filtering in Convex queries (server-side)
- All phase transitions via Convex mutations
